{
  "name": "memory-session",
  "about": "Where an open document's memory goes over an ordinary session: open, prepared at idle, played, stopped, then fifteen X-sheet pastes (each a structural edit, so each pushes a whole-document copy onto undo). Read the app's 'memory' marks in the run's log: still and tile caches, compose buffers, undo depth, managed heap, process total.",
